# 13. CLIP AND SCENE PLAYBACK RULES

Define the behavior unambiguously.

One active clip per track in Session View.

Different tracks can play different clips simultaneously.

Launching another clip in the same track replaces the current clip at the chosen quantization boundary.

Launching a scene schedules its contained clips simultaneously.

Stop actions follow global quantization where appropriate, with an immediate stop-all option.

All clips derive timing from the same project transport.

Clip loops must continue seamlessly.

Clips with different lengths must coexist correctly.

Example:

- Track 1 loops every 1 bar.
- Track 2 loops every 4 bars.
- Track 3 loops every 8 bars.

All three must stay synchronized indefinitely without accumulating drift.

Playback must continue while:

- Browsing instruments.
- Opening the MIDI editor.
- Switching tracks.
- Changing parameters.
- Viewing project settings.

Avoid resetting the transport on navigation.

